hi  everyone welcome to this live session by  simply learn  today's topic is final year project tips  in today's session we'll give you all  the tips that will help you ace your  final year project  but before we begin i'd like to thank  our viewers on youtube and facebook for  actively participating in these sessions  so let's wait for a while for people to  tune in  once again i welcome everyone to this  live session by simply learn  if you have any questions do feel free  to leave them in the chat section and we  will be happy to answer them  also make sure to subscribe to our  channel and hit the bell icon to never  miss an update  now let's get started we have 7 vital  tips that will help you complete your  final year project successfully  we will look into each one of these tips  individually so without further ado  let's start with our first tip  first and foremost choosing the right  topic holds paramount importance  with the number of options available  today this decision can be overwhelming  you must ensure that the topics you  choose are related to your field of  study and that is of interest to you  you will be required to deep dive into  your topic hence you must choose a topic  that interests you  it is recommended that you have a topic  that has a strong motive  in many cases projects that help mankind  is highly recommended  in addition to that research and choose  topics that aren't common and  traditional  this will help you stand out from the  others  now let's look at a few examples of  projects related to the different  branches of engineering  on your screens you can see the popular  trending projects for computer science  and it  we have chat bots chatbots are getting  widely popular these days and are being  extensively used to solve customer  problems  we have face detection that is used in  companies such as facebook google  and ibm you can also focus on creating  projects related to some current events  such as predicting coronavirus cases  or predicting the upcoming u.s elections  you can create a search engine that  would return relevant links based on  your search term  another interesting project you can do  is to perform sentiment analysis using  python or  r now let's see a few electrical and  electronics projects that might interest  ec  or tripoli students you can create a  simple bluetooth controlled electronic  home appliances project  where you can control different  electrical appliances and electronic  devices using an android device with the  help of bluetooth  technology you can use radio frequency  technology and build a metal detector  robotic system that can help  identify metals in the ground inside a  bag etc  you can build a 5 volt regulated dc  supply from 220 ac to charge  mobiles as well as the power sources for  digital circuits  breadboard circuits ics microcontrollers  etc  electricity is one of the most important  resources and it must be utilized  carefully  you can create a microcontroller based  project that automatically turns on or  off the lights in a room a project on  micro inverters can be used to power  light loads such as night lamps and  cordless telephones  you can modify it into a powerful  inverter by adding more mosfets  now let's discuss a few of the popular  mechanical projects  we would like to remind you that these  projects are not the only ones that you  need to choose  there are a lot of other interesting  projects that you can opt for  in your final year here first we have a  3d printer  you can build a 3d printer machine that  has additive manufacturing techniques in  which 3d objects can be printed with the  help of computer aided design software  you can create a compressed air engine  that does mechanical work by expanding  compressed air  reducing the cost of vehicle production  and consumption of fossil fuels  using modern tools and software such as  autodesk showcase  lightwave 3d alias autodesk and bread  you can create 3d visualizations and  design vehicles  finally we have a conveyor system  project that supports mechanical  handling equipment to move  objects from one location to another  let's now move on to the next step we  have  and that is to choose the right guide  a project guide plays a major role in  defining the success of the project  he or she should be a good mentor who  goes the extra mile for helping you with  your project  the guide you choose should be a  knowledgeable subject matter expert in  the same field as your project  this way even if you get stuck or run  out of ideas your project guide will be  able to help you with it smoothly  it will be an added advantage if your  guide is carrying out research in the  same domain or if he or she has  published research papers in the past  you must be able to add extra weightage  to your project by utilizing your guides  experience and knowledge  in addition to choosing the right guide  also make sure that if it is a group  project  choose the right set of team members to  work with choosing the right members who  are cooperative and equally hard working  is very crucial  so the next step that you need to take  care of seriously is planning your  project  well this might sound very generic but  it is crucial throughout the  process once you have finalized your  project topic  and the guide you have to make extensive  plans as to how to go about the entire  process  you must have a project plan which  covers the goal research  requirements cost estimations  implementation and presentation  planning the project beforehand will  help you streamline your process  and in turn save you from last minute  confusions  make sure to create a plan keeping in  mind the deadlines  it is advised that you break down your  project into faces and then execute them  step by step  a strong project plan can yield better  results than you can imagine  the next step we have for you is to read  all the existing research papers  in the same field as your project you  might wonder how this will help you  well there are several advantages to  this by reading the existing research  papers that are closely related to your  project you will get an idea as to what  content is already there  and what is lacking you need to make  sure that your project has additional  and new information  from the already existing ones for this  purpose you need to be aware of all the  research done previously  reading research papers will also give  you an outline as to how you should  proceed with your work  and what are the kinds of content that  have to be highlighted  moving on to our fifth tip that is to  publish a research paper  publishing a research paper is one of  the ways you can add credibility to your  project  it also gives you more confidence while  presenting your project  in a lot of cases research papers can  also open doors to new opportunities  once you are done writing your research  paper make sure to reference it properly  proofread and  edit check your research paper for  repetitions grammatical errors quotation  rules obeyed and so on  not to forget that research papers add a  great amount of weightage to your resume  the cutouts that you see here are a few  examples of research papers published in  leading journals and professional  associations  related to multiple technologies and  research domains  such as quantum computing augmented  reality  wireless sensor networks axial turbines  and others  it is highly recommended to publish a  paper in peer-reviewed journals that  gives international recognition  for an individual department university  and institutions  it helps in enrolling for higher  education at reputed institutes  you can apply for a career in research  and teaching positions as well  moving on to our next step the next step  you have to keep in mind is to implement  and test your project  well before presenting your project make  sure to implement it and then test it  well  by doing this even if there are any  errors you can fix them  there may be some trials and errors at  first but you would need to keep going  after your project is built it is time  to test it  you can do this with some test cases in  order to check if your project is  yielding the expected results or not  you must ensure that it is aligned with  your project goal and there shouldn't be  any deviations  and a final project tip to you is a  strong presentation  and visualization of your project  there is no point in having worked so  much if you are unable to deliver your  project well on the final day  hence it is of utmost importance that  you're well versed with your project and  make a good presentation on it  while making your presentation keep in  mind that it has to be interesting with  all the required information  making use of data visualization in your  presentation will be an  added advantage and the project results  will be delivered in a crystal clear  manner  during a project presentation there will  be a number of questions from the panel  you should calmly and carefully answer  the questions asked  you can master the art of presentation  with good practice  there you go those were important tips  in order to successfully complete your  final year project  with that we have come to the end of  this live session by simply learn  i hope it was informative and useful if  you think we missed out on any important  tips then please feel free to put it in  the comments section of the video  also don't forget to subscribe to our  channel thank you for watching and keep  learning  you

